0292: DSI command sets as Android sends them: memory-fetch DMA, batched to the "last" packet
(new bsd/dev/negroni_dsi.c; hooks in NegroniBacklight.cpp after 0268; NegroniFramebuffer.cpp 0259 mode 1 HS)

Android (display-drivers dsi_display.c:820-858, dsi_ctrl.c:1615-1752, dsi_ctrl_hw_cmn.c:870-918)
fetches DCS commands from a 4 KiB uncached buffer (DSI_CTRL_CMD_FETCH_MEMORY) and sends every
packet up to one without the batch flag (DT flags 0x40) in one DMA. 0250 sent one FIFO DMA per
packet behind a 20 ms MDP-busy wait each (62 packets per 0259 timing switch).

negronifb_dsidma=1: negroni_dsi_dcs_set_ex (0268; every set: 0259 VRR, 0268 on-command) goes
through the memory DMA inside 0268's set lock, from 0268's command buffer (0xbaafc000, the end of the
UEFI splash region, write-combined; the first 4 KiB): DMA_CMD_OFFSET/LENGTH, SW trigger,
CMD_DMA_DONE poll, reset_cmd_fifo, the registers as found; one MDP-busy wait per set; a packet with
a wait ends its batch. =2: single DCS writes too. Default 0 (0250/0268 per-packet path). A DMA that
does not finish turns the memory DMA off for the boot (also 0268's long packets) and the rest of
the set goes out packet by packet. Logs: "NEGRONI DSI: memory DMA (negronifb_dsidma=N): command sets from 0x...",
"NEGRONI DSI: set of N bytes: N packets in N memory DMAs (N bytes), HS|LP, N us, rc 0".
0259 mode 1 (min-fps set) now defaults to HS like the DT state (live.dts 35650); negronifb_vrr_hs=0
restores LP.

